: Early voting in SC tops 363K heading into weekend, doubling last midterm","note":"The verdict is our like-for-like reading of the claim (grade I); the evidence cites its own grades."},{"value":{"outlet":"WIS-TV","date":"2026-10-22","headline":"Over 363K early votes cast in South Carolina","claim":"Turnout highest in Greenville, Charleston, Richland","cmp":"none","verdict":"holds","evidence":"Counts match SCEC file [V]. Greenville (a Republican county) leads the state [R Post and Courier]."},"grade":"I","as_of":"2026-10-22","source_url":"https://wistv.com/2026/10/22/over-280k-early-votes-cast-so-far-south-carolina","source":"WIS-TV: Over 363K early votes cast in South Carolina","note":"The verdict is our like-for-like reading of the claim (grade I); the evidence cites its own grades."},{"value":{"outlet":"Winthrop Poll (Scott Huffmon) substack","date":"2026-10-23","headline":"2026 Early Voting in SC compared to 2024 & 2022","claim":"SC early vote nears 2/3 of 2022 total EV share after 4 days; Democratic enthusiasm trickling down","cmp":"2022 and 2024 by day, % of registered","verdict":"overstated","evidence":"Comparison basis is right (per-registered, by day) but the enthusiasm inference has no partisan data behind it; SC early-vote files carry no race/party. Mail ballots (the only race-coded data) are 26.5% Black so far vs 24.2% at 2022 final [V], a small shift on 26,106 ballots."},"grade":"I","as_of":"2026-10-23","source_url":"https://winthroppoll.substack.com/p/2026-early-voting-in-sc-compared","source":"Winthrop Poll (Scott Huffmon) substack: 2026 Early Voting in SC compared to 2024 & 2022","note":"The verdict is our like-for-like reading of the claim (grade I); the evidence cites its own grades."}]},"races":{"rows":[{"id":"SEN-SC","cls":"SEN","office":"U.S. Senate (Class 2)","dist":"","D":"Annie Andrews","R":"Darline Graham","other":"Mark Hackett (Constitution); Kasie Whitener (Libertarian)","inc":"Darline Graham","open":false,"pres24":"R+17.9","rating":"Likel